From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Scott Jordan <scott@spaceshipcreative.com>
Date: Thu, 8 Oct 2026 05:14:47 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 09/25] Run FLASHINFER_MLA_SPARSE_SM90 on SM12x through
 FlashInfer FA2

Source: MiaAI-Lab/GLM-5.3-Flash-NVFP4-Dual-DGX-Spark,
  glm53-flash_SM121.py, step bake_sm90_wrapper_for_gb10 (MIT,
  Copyright (c) 2026 MiaAI-Lab). Taken from the verbatim copy vendored in
  kindlingai/glm-5.3-flash-gx10 image/patches/ at c748079 (with
  LICENSE.MiaAI-Lab). Turned from anchor replacements into a diff against
  v0.31.0; all three anchors matched v0.31.0 exactly once.
Upstream status: absent. No vLLM PR enables the SM90 sparse-MLA backend
  on capability 12.

The SM90 sparse-MLA backend wraps FlashInfer's BatchMLAPagedAttention.
Its FA3 kernel needs Hopper (wgmma), but the FA2 kernel behind the same
wrapper is portable to sm_12x, and the backend already covers NoPE MLA
(kpe in {0, 64}). On GB10 this is the only FlashInfer sparse-MLA path
that keeps a plain fp8_e4m3 KV cache (512 B/token rather than the 656 B
fp8_ds_mla rows SM120 forces) and dense-MHA prefill, which
FLASHINFER_MLA_SPARSE_SM120 lacks.

- supports_compute_capability accepts major 12 as well as 9.
- _SM90State picks backend="fa3" on SM90 and "fa2" elsewhere. FA2 and
  FA3 share MLAPlan/MLAPlanInfo (include/flashinfer/attention/
  scheduler.cuh), and the FA2 kernel treats kv_end <= kv_start as an
  empty work item, so v0.31.0's sync-free plan with the device-side
  kv_end clamp (#58684) carries over unchanged.
- The ckv_scale_arr feature gate (FlashInfer >= 0.6.18) applies only to
  fp8 KV; a bf16 cache does not need it.

FP8 KV on SM12x additionally needs two FlashInfer 0.7.0.post1 fixes
shipped as separate site-packages patches: the FA2 fp8 gate in
_fa_common.py (major != 9) and the fp8 CTA_TILE_KV in mla.cuh (32 does
not fit GB10's ~100 KB smem/SM). bf16 KV runs on stock FlashInfer.

Selection is unchanged by this commit: the backend is reachable on SM12x
only through --attention-backend FLASHINFER_MLA_SPARSE_SM90.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 .../mla/flashinfer_mla_sparse_sm90.py         | 19 ++++++++++++++-----
 1 file changed, 14 insertions(+), 5 deletions(-)

diff --git a/vllm/v1/attention/backends/mla/flashinfer_mla_sparse_sm90.py b/vllm/v1/attention/backends/mla/flashinfer_mla_sparse_sm90.py
index a5f7757d3..c8f063fe4 100644
--- a/vllm/v1/attention/backends/mla/flashinfer_mla_sparse_sm90.py
+++ b/vllm/v1/attention/backends/mla/flashinfer_mla_sparse_sm90.py
@@ -8,6 +8,10 @@ and FP8 E4M3 KV caches on SM90 with in-kernel dequantization: the FP8 cache
 is read directly (half the bf16 HBM traffic) and converted to BF16 in shared
 memory, while queries stay BF16 (no query quantization).
 
+On SM12x (GB10 / DGX Spark) the same wrapper runs FlashInfer's portable FA2
+kernel instead of FA3. FP8 KV there needs a FlashInfer whose FA2 MLA path
+accepts SM12x and fits its ~100 KB shared memory per SM.
+
 Sparsity rides the same trick the FA-based sparse backend uses: with
 ``page_size=1`` the per-token top-k slot indices ARE the page table, so each
 query token becomes one varlen batch row whose ``kv_indices`` slice is its
@@ -176,7 +180,9 @@ class FlashInferMLASparseSM90Backend(AttentionBackend):
 
     @classmethod
     def supports_compute_capability(cls, capability: DeviceCapability) -> bool:
-        return capability.major == 9
+        # SM12x (GB10, RTX 50xx/PRO) runs the portable FA2 kernel; see
+        # _SM90State. FA3 stays Hopper-only.
+        return capability.major in (9, 12)
 
     @classmethod
     def supports_combination(
@@ -191,10 +197,10 @@ class FlashInferMLASparseSM90Backend(AttentionBackend):
         use_mm_prefix: bool,
         device_capability: DeviceCapability,
     ) -> str | None:
-        if not has_flashinfer_sm90_nope_mla():
+        if kv_cache_dtype in _FP8_KV_DTYPES and not has_flashinfer_sm90_nope_mla():
             return (
-                "FLASHINFER_MLA_SPARSE_SM90 requires FlashInfer with SM90 "
-                "MLA support (ckv_scale_arr in "
+                "FLASHINFER_MLA_SPARSE_SM90 fp8 KV requires FlashInfer with "
+                "SM90 MLA support (ckv_scale_arr in "
                 "BatchMLAPagedAttentionWrapper.run, FlashInfer >= 0.6.18)"
             )
         if not use_sparse:
@@ -271,6 +277,9 @@ class _SM90State:
             (max_tokens,), topk_width, dtype=torch.int32, device=device
         )
         self.kv_indptr = torch.zeros(max_tokens + 1, dtype=torch.int32, device=device)
+        # FA3 (wgmma) is Hopper-only; FA2 is portable to SM12x. Both use the
+        # same MLAPlanInfo layout, so the kv_end clamp below applies to both.
+        backend = "fa3" if torch.cuda.get_device_capability(device)[0] == 9 else "fa2"
         self.wrapper = BatchMLAPagedAttentionWrapper(
             self.workspace,
             qo_indptr=torch.zeros(max_tokens + 1, dtype=torch.int32, device=device),
@@ -278,7 +287,7 @@ class _SM90State:
             kv_indices=self.kv_indices,
             kv_len_arr=self.kv_len_arr,
             use_cuda_graph=True,
-            backend="fa3",
+            backend=backend,
         )
         self._arange_cpu = torch.arange(self.max_tokens + 1, dtype=torch.int32)
         self._qo_cpu = torch.empty(self.max_tokens + 1, dtype=torch.int32)
